cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite both the manuscript and the archived software release."
title: "hnscc-tls-signatures: analysis code and derived data for Tertiary lymphoid structure gene signatures are not interchangeable in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis pipeline, derived patient-level data, and complete result
  tables and figures for a multi-signature transcriptomic analysis of tertiary
  lymphoid structure (TLS) gene signatures in 438 patients with head and neck
  squamous cell carcinoma from TCGA-HNSC. The study shows that chemokine-based
  TLS signatures are nearly redundant with one another and correlate almost as
  strongly with a generic T cell-inflamed signature as with each other, that the
  consensus score tracks immune checkpoint and regulatory T cell programmes more
  strongly than TLS structural features, and that its prognostic value is
  cut-off dependent and not independent of stage and age.
